:\n\n- The left endpoint $-5$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $[\\,.$\n\n- The right endpoint $-2$ is *not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $)\\,.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding interval is\n\n$$\nx\\in [-5,-2).\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c4ee4f-ba6e-5665-9290-8b399dab05fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (- 3\\sqrt{3}, - 3\\sqrt{5}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502545} {:answer/id #uuid "878d18fa-fe79-5b4f-b429-ccb016dcbe57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 3\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502586} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5972e8-c37f-5a62-9315-53aaf2189e9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 3\\sqrt{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502598} {:answer/id #uuid "b4af30b2-d791-5f55-84fa-082f4bd2c37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 3\\sqrt{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502601} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9a4b14-be08-5841-b520-243baea71da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 3\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4af30b2-d791-5f55-84fa-082f4bd2c37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 3\\sqrt{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502601} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f079c91-9df9-5a0f-9f37-1a86b0823146" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "006e3aaa-0e14-54c2-a59f-f0b8ca035512" :question/problem "The inequality $- 3\\sqrt{5} < u \\le - 3\\sqrt{3}$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every interval can be expressed as an inequality. We use the following notations:\n\n- Paren