 t < - 2\\sqrt{6}\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $- 3\\sqrt{5}$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $[$.\n- The right endpoint $- 2\\sqrt{6}$ *is not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $) $.\n\nTherefore, the interval that corresponds to the given inequality is\n\n$$\nt ∈ [- 3\\sqrt{5}, - 2\\sqrt{6})\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502620 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19150541-c12f-528e-a489-a57cbb42c473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [-13, 3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502546} {:answer/id #uuid "32122061-15d5-5436-9654-3f005d8bcac7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (-13, 3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502555} {:answer/id #uuid "97f08df8-69db-524d-baf6-20dc27174fdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [3, -13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502591} {:answer/id #uuid "e06630fb-c6fb-5c22-b7e5-4c3f15ec6288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ (-13, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502619} {:answer/id #uuid "fb2dcc3a-11fe-5ce8-b575-7f990950066c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [-13, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb2dcc3a-11fe-5ce8-b575-7f990950066c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u ∈ [-13, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502627} :answer-field/id #uuid "0db57638-ec92-50c7-a1ba-0cc2855a43c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e79a1ce7-6ab1-5be1-897f-c640c7ff5365" :question/problem "The inequality $-13 \\le u < 3$ can be expressed in interval notation as" :question/worked-solution "Every interval can be expressed as an inequality. We use the following notations:\n\n- Parentheses ${\\color{red}{(}}\\phantom{0} \\phantom{0}{\\color{red}{)}}$ to indicate that the endpoints are *not* included.\n- Brackets ${\\color{blue}{[}}\\phantom{0}\\phantom{0}{\\color{blue}{]}}$ to indicate that the endpoints *are* included.\n\nFor the given inequality\n\n$$\n-13 \\le u < 3\n$$\n\nwe note the following:\n\n- The left endpoint $-13$ *is* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $[$.\n- The right endpoint $3$ *is not* included in the interval. Therefore, we use $) $.\n\nTherefore, the interval that corresponds to the given inequality is\n\n$$\nu ∈ [-13, 3)\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Translating Between Half-Open Intervals and Inequalities"}]}
